            {
              "id": "DEP-KNOWN-ADVISORY",
              "name": "DepKnownAdvisory",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "block-buffer 0.10.4 is affected by GHSA-qwgh-2vcv-g2f7"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "dependencies",
                  "known_vulnerable_component"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.0"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "OSV.dev reports GHSA-qwgh-2vcv-g2f7 for crates.io package block-buffer at version 0.10.4: block_buffer: panic corrupts inline buffer position. The advisory names no affected functions, so reachability was not determined. Upgrade to a fixed version (none published yet; see the advisory for mitigations). Advisory data comes from OSV.dev at the recorded time. Reachability is judged from names, not a call graph: the affected functions the advisory lists against the identifiers in the audited product code, a Cargo feature it says is off by default against the audited manifests, the platforms it lists against the declared Rust targets. Indirect calls (traits, macros, other dependencies) are not followed."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "OSV.dev reports GHSA-qwgh-2vcv-g2f7 for crates.io package block-buffer at version 0.10.4: block_buffer: panic corrupts inline buffer position. The advisory names no affected functions, so reachability was not determined. Upgrade to a fixed version (none published yet; see the advisory for mitigations). Advisory data comes from OSV.dev at the recorded time. Reachability is judged from names, not a call graph: the affected functions the advisory lists against the identifiers in the audited product code, a Cargo feature it says is off by default against the audited manifests, the platforms it lists against the declared Rust targets. Indirect calls (traits, macros, other dependencies) are not followed."
              },
